00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.930
And now back to the show,

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.960
remember our friend religious
scholar, Dr. Eichler-Levine,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.090
who's passionate defense of Disney adults

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.700
inspired this video
series in the first place.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.980
Well, she's far from the
first person to explore

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.690
the possibility that Disney

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.630
might constitute a modern day religion.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.570
Way back in 1934, author Ian Forrester

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.740
went so far as to argue that
Mickey is everybody's god.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.477
Meanwhile, scholar Richard
Foglesong called Disney

00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:33.780
"The Vatican with mouse ears".

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.370
But in order to really determine

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.110
if Disney is a full blown faith,

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.310
we first need to think about

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.590
what makes something a
religion to begin with.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.700
For our purposes,

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.620
we're gonna use anthropologist
Clifford Geertz's

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.960
popular definition from 1973,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.410
which outlines five stipulations
to define religion as:

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.660
One, a system of symbols.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.970
Two, about the nature of things.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.030
Three, that inculcate
dispositions for behavior.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.550
Four, through ritual and
cultural performance.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.220
Five, so that the
conceptions held by the group

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.690
are taken as real.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.010
Addressing the first piece.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.960
A system of symbols look no further

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.250
than Mickey Mouse himself,

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.120
who has become a worldwide
symbol of innocence.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.370
And the United States market
researchers have found

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.980
he has a 97% recognition rate.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.310
Making him more recognizable
than Santa Claus.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.177
As cultural critic, Henry Jeroh notes,

00:03:22.177 --> 00:03:24.270
"The cultural iconography of Disney,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.600
renders it a purveyor of
innocence and family fun."

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.190
He adds that through its films,

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.667
parks and endless merchandising,

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:33.600
"Disney becomes a symbol
for the security and romance

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.450
of the small town America of yesteryear"

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.250
From the iconic Cinderella's castle,

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.590
representing enchantment
and dreams coming true,

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:43.950
to barbershop quartets
strolling down Main Street, USA,

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.510
Disney is rife with symbolism,
not unlike that of religion.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.370
They do some of this by operating as

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.650
what DePaul University
professor, Michael Budde,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.050
might call "symbolic predators".

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.870
That is appropriating existing imagery

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.610
from traditional religions.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.490
Indeed like the sun shining
over Simba's kingdom

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.110
echoes of world religions appear

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.560
throughout Disney properties.

00:04:06.555 --> 00:04:07.710
Take the concept of the circle of life,

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.840
which is deeply rooted in Hinduism,

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.880
according to journalist, Mark Penske.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.250
Or Snow White, taking
a bite from an apple,

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.930
like you know who.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.450
Heck Penske points out that in Pinocchio,

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.340
when Geppeto falls to his knees

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.590
to ask an undefined deity for help,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.990
a fairy appears conveniently decked out

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.690
in the Virgin Mary's
trademark shade of blue.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.280
Still let's be clear,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.430
explicit references are largely
absent from Disney movies.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.630
This was intentional.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.633
Disney biographer, Bob
Thomas, notes that Walt Disney

00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:38.490
made the strategic business decision

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.080
to keep religion out of his films,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.370
in order to make them marketable

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.680
to the widest international audience.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.750
And yet, there's still
an argument to be made

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.880
for the second qualification for religion

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.620
about the nature of things.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.530
Disney movies may not feature
an explicit God figure,

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.960
but many have argued that
Disney effectively poached

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.420
a lot of Judeo-Christian ideology,

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.270
while scrubbing out the
actual divinity stuff.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.137
As Penske explained back in 2004,

00:05:02.137 --> 00:05:04.980
"There is relatively little
explicit Judeo-Christian

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.530
symbolism or substance in 70 years

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.240
of Disney's animated features,

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.910
despite the frequent, almost pervasive use

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.390
of a theological vocabulary:
words, such as faith,

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:19.050
believe, miracle, blessing,
sacrifice, and divine.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.420
It seems a contradiction,
portraying consistent

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.740
Judeo-Christian values

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.590
without sectarian or even godly context,

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.080
the fruits without the roots."

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.940
He points out that Disney
effectively preaches

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.910
the Protestant work ethic
minus the whole God thing.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.310
Exemplifying the argument that hard work

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.910
leads to upward social
mobility, no matter what.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.710
Echoes of the David and Goliath story

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.660
frequently pulsate through the films,

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:46.290
with the poor and downtrodden
always eventually triumphing

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.390
over the powerful and corrupt.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:52.110
As Penske summarizes,
"Good is always rewarded;

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:53.460
evil is always punished.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.410
Faith is an essential element,

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.430
faith in yourself,

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.370
and, even more, faith in
something greater than yourself,

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:00.690
some higher power.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.690
Optimism and hard work
complete the basic canon."

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.200
Penske dubs this Disney
ethos "Secular Toonism",

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.870
explaining that in place of
God working his divine magic,

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:13.200
Disney uses magical
creatures doing magic magic,

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.210
you know, fairies and fairy godmothers,

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.830
genie and ice queen, sea
witches and land witches.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.727
In this way scholar Kathy
Merlock Jackson writes,

00:06:21.727 --> 00:06:24.330
"Magic becomes a way to
empower the powerless,

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.270
just like God does in so many
classic biblical stories."

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.820
So part two pretty much checks out.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.570
Part three inculcating
dispositions for certain behaviors.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:36.690
We're gonna set aside for now
and return to momentarily.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.940
So we've established
that Disney essentially

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:42.120
created and maintained a
consistent system of symbols

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.550
about the nature of
things across its films,

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.470
parks and other products.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:50.010
But how are those messages
imparted onto its believers?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.750
Well as author Richard Corliss

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.877
speculated in a 1988
issue of Time Magazine,

00:06:54.877 --> 00:06:57.150
"Walt Disney's philosophy
may as well have been

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:00.870
the Jesuit credo of 'give me
a child before he is seven,

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.940
and he will be mine for life'."

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.227
Indeed Disney said as
much, declaring that,

00:07:05.227 --> 00:07:08.130
"I think of a child's
mind as a blank book.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.660
During the first years of his life,

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.820
much will be written on the pages.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.080
The quality of that writing

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.330
will affect his life profoundly."

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.409
By his own logic then,

00:07:16.409 --> 00:07:18.900
Disney has been for multiple generations,

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.510
scribbling all over those blank minds.

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:24.900
With children spending more
time consuming Disney films

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.850
than they do with organized religion.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.460
And of course, as many of
us grow out of childhood

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.990
and into our teens and adulthood,

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.080
Disney is right there to
accompany us on our journeys.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.660
Except this time with
Jedis, and superheroes,

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.420
and bounty hunters, until
life gets so depressing

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.550
that we need the talking animals again.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:43.980
And then we come to part
four of our definition,

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.140
ritual and cultural performance

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.850
by far the most salient place

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.800
where the rituals of Disney consolidate

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.900
is, of course, at its theme parks.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.030
According to Harper's magazine's index,

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.940
an estimated 70% of Americans
have been to one of them,

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.620
which is probably the only thing

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.620
70% of Americans have in common.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.380
These larger than life locations
are seen by some scholars

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.710
as akin to sacred spaces where
visitors make a pilgrimage,

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:11.010
not unlike that of Jews to
Jerusalem, or Muslims to Mecca,

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.650
or American Irish Catholics
to the Guinness brewery

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.180
at St. James Gate, Dublin.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.550
Fittingly Disney's parks are absent

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.920
of the unholy banalities of real life

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.770
like litter, or swearing, or frowning.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.990
Religion scholar, Mircea Eliadi,

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.850
describes the importance people of faith

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:28.800
ascribe to so-called sacred spaces,

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.430
i.e. places that seem to
exist in a sacred time,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.890
that is when the world
was young and Edenic.

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:37.590
In these spaces, myth and
ritual help worshipers

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:40.620
by recalibrating life toward the divine.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.870
As scholars, Eric Mazur and Tara Koda,

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.450
summarize in their book, "The
Happiest Place on Earth".

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.970
Notably as Drew points out Disney too

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.620
exists outside of time,

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:52.290
Hell, Disney reportedly
removed all alarm clocks

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.300
from its hotels in 2016.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.760
More importantly, the
parks have no references

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.520
to the present, a few
references towards the future,

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.740
but mostly seem to exist in a past

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.190
that somehow approximates
Eisenhower's conservative America.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.190
That is a time when the world was young.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.440
Indeed Disney world was
attracting the nostalgia

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.170
of baby boomer parents long
before it became the site

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.180
of their millennial children's weddings.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.790
Missing, of course, is anything
unpleasant about that era,

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.020
like the Red Scare, or
racism, or barbiturates.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.930
In frontier land, the American
frontier is mythologized

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.940
as a place of courage and adventure,

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.850
making the brutal genocide
committed against native people

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:32.220
on those lands a brief footnote.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.770
American history is further
glorified and sanitized

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:36.840
in places like the hall of the presidents,

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.870
where ugly parts of
history like say Watergate

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:42.240
or Iran Contra are ignored

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:45.120
as an animatronic Abe
Lincoln in Christ like glory

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.010
returns to life.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.410
Historian Mike Wallace
calls this commercialization

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.720
of the past, Mickey Mouse history.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.110
A narrative written "without
classes, conflict or crime,

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:59.070
a world of continuous consumption,
a supermarket of fun."

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.770
Innocence effectively
becomes a magic eraser

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:04.740
cleansing history of
its less savory moments.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.720
And these Disney
narratives all come to life

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:07.980
in its holy sites.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.260
Where rituals like riding Splash Mountain,

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.240
or watching sunset
parades down Main Street,

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.520
or getting your picture
taken with the characters

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:18.270
for a hefty fee, all
provide joy and catharsis.

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.070
In these spaces, religious scholar,

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.157
Peter Gardella writes,

00:10:21.157 --> 00:10:24.870
"Magical beings like Tinkerbell
and Mickey Mouse abound,

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.450
and many shows imply that such beings

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.130
might help ordinary people."

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:31.590
Gardella calls this "trans-theism"

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:34.110
or "the provisional
acceptance of many gods

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.480
with an implied underlying oneness"

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.740
As with a religious service,

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:40.500
your sense of possibilities
for your life are expanded

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.750
through promises of divine intervention,

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:45.990
or at least the ear of a
sympathetic fairy godmother.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:49.470
Giroux describes Disney as
a privatized, homogenous,

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.790
and risk free city.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.017
Whereas critic Elaine Rapping points out,

00:10:53.017 --> 00:10:56.040
"No trace of anything
non-comodified, non-simulated,

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.330
non-regulated non-smiley-faced,
is visible or reachable"

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.740
As with other sacred sites,

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:04.710
the sense of effortless
magic is facilitated as much

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.860
by what you don't see as by what you do.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:10.290
A tour of the Pope's bathroom
might kind of ruin the vibe

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.790
of the Vatican after all.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.040
Similarly, there's a virtual absence

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.840
of anything non magical at Disney,

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.180
most especially, visible labor.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.170
Disney employees, sorry,
we mean cast members,

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.180
use underground tunnels to transport

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.760
food, products, and waste.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:29.220
As Giroux concludes,
"Through the use of public

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:32.160
visual space, i.e. parks
like Magic Kingdom,

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.050
Disney's network of power relations

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.300
promotes the construction
of an all encompassing

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:39.630
world of enchantment,
allegedly free from ideology,

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.370
politics and power".

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:44.160
That's in spite of the fact
that political lobbying

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.840
is the reason that Disney World

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:47.310
was able to exist for so long

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:50.370
as a self-governing
independent special district.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.890
The park paints itself as
a place of transcendence

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:56.460
of elevation beyond the
mundanity of everyday life,

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.477
which brings us to stipulation five.

00:11:58.477 --> 00:12:01.080
"So that the conceptions held by the group

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.850
are taken as real."

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:05.430
Now, we're obviously not
saying that Disney adults

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:08.640
literally wish upon stars
or, work hard at their jobs

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.130
just because seven dwarves
of various dispositions

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:11.963
told them to,

00:12:11.963 --> 00:12:15.120
but Disney's grand narrative
of spiritual uplift,

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.730
moral truth, and endless nostalgia

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.680
seems to be taken at face value

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.630
or filtered through the fervor

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.610
with which Disney adults
express themselves.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.680
Disney adults may not pay tzedakah

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.240
at the temple of Tinkerbell,

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.150
but one popular Disney
world vacation tip site,

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.280
suggests that two adults have to cough up

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:36.570
between 1,900 and $2,800 to visit Disney,

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.240
which I'd call a healthy tithe.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:41.310
Meanwhile, according
to the Washington post

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:42.810
Disney continues to hike prices

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.390
as much as five to 10% each year,

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:49.860
which is fine because wages
go up at the same rate, right?

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.810
That's how economics work.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:54.270
Viewing Disney World as a
site for rights of passage

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.400
like weddings or bar and bat mitzvahs,

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.620
cements the sense of faith fans have

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.900
in the sanctity of its ethos.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.540
Now let's return to
stipulation number three,

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.820
inculcating dispositions for behavior.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:09.060
What, if any, sort of behavior
does the Disney empire

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.650
encourage in its supplicants?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:11.850
You might be surprised actually

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.040
that we haven't really brought it up yet,

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.820
starts with C synonym for eat,
that's right, consumption,

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:18.960
and lots of it.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.457
As American studies scholar,
Eric Smoodin puts it,

00:13:21.457 --> 00:13:23.850
"Disney constructs
childhood so as to make it

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:26.310
entirely compatible with consumerism",

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:29.040
and it does so in the hopes
of creating lifelong patrons

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.200
of Disney entertainment
and related products.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.960
Though, it's not the only
company to attempt such a feat,

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:35.437
Mazur and Koda argue that,

00:13:35.437 --> 00:13:37.260
"Because of its market penetration,

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.580
it's integrated marketing

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.530
and its access to many levels of culture

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:41.820
through its corporate network,

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.380
Disney is uniquely suited

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.690
for the religification of its commodity."

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.850
This is important because as Giroux notes,

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:50.827
in our world of rapidly
evolving mass communication,

00:13:50.827 --> 00:13:53.100
"Pop culture is a central
way for young people

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.480
to learn about themselves,

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:57.060
their relationship to others
and the larger world."

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.820
He argues that Disney is
perfectly suited for a world

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.740
where democracy has
come to be less defined

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:04.740
by civic engagement than by
the freedom to consume freely,

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.090
and be entertained.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:09.360
Disney, he explains, prime
children to relate to themselves

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.160
as consumers, before citizens,

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.440
as individuals pursuing self-interest,

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.630
rather than members of
communities pursuing

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.190
any sort of collective good.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:20.040
And then carry that
self-perception into adulthood.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.350
Nowhere is this more
evident than a Disney world,

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:24.690
whereas Giroux explains,
"Consumption becomes

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.730
the unifying force through which families

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.170
organize themselves.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.840
Disney theme parks, not only
provide middle class families

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.060
with an upbeat version
of the American past.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.030
They give such entertainment,
the force of civic duty.

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:38.250
Encouraging spectatorship and passivity,

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.110
Disney appropriates nostalgia,

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.880
simply to maximize consumption

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.920
in the interest of fun and commerce."

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.040
All at the side of Mickey
mouse popsicles, of course.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.930
Now, given Disney's ability to fulfill

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.900
all five stipulations of
Geertz's definition of religion.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:54.840
It's easy to conclude that it is in fact

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:58.080
functioning like a religion,
even if unintentionally.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.670
But there's still a bit more to unpack.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:02.640
See, most religions ask
us to sacrifice things

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:06.510
in exchange for say salvation,
or God's good graces.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:08.910
We're supposed to give our
money to houses of worship,

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:12.300
or charities, or spend part
of our weekends in prayer,

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.340
or deny ourselves the
pleasure of red meat,

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:15.750
or avoid masturbating

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:17.580
so the Pope doesn't show up to our house

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.440
and glue our palms to a cross.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.600
Religions also typically ask us to strive

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.280
to abide by an ethical code,

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:25.440
and repent when we fail to do so.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.290
But Disney's pitch is a bit more simple,

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.510
as Phil Vicher, co-founder
of Veggie Tails,

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.760
persuasively argues,
"Disney has wrapped up

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.070
and sold America what
people wanted to hear,

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.560
which was 'give us the upside of religion

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.750
without the obligation of religion'."

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.550
That is, like a lot of businesses,

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:44.340
Disney offers us enlightenment
through consumption

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:47.010
without asking us to do any
of the pesky self examination

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:49.230
that traditional religion might require.

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:51.990
The difference is, it just
happens to have a lot more power,

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:54.450
and of course, a lot more real estate

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:57.120
than most of the other
people trying to sell you.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.940
At their parks, we can
enjoy all the spiritual

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.950
and ecstatic feeling of religious worship,

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:05.250
without having any of the
moral or ethical responsibility

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.260
that religion imposes upon us.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:10.740
Disney's ideology is
ultimately pretty hollow,

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.350
and yet its cultural
reach is so expansive.

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:16.320
Its appeals to childhood
innocence so persuasive,

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:17.790
that we can easily forget.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.040
It's not a value driven benevolent entity

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.140
striving to uplift its followers.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:25.740
It's a profit driven
multinational corporation

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.040
as Giroux puts it, "Innocence
serves as a rhetorical device

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.800
that cleanses the Disney image
of the messiness of commerce,

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.240
ideology, and power."

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:36.270
That is to say, marketing
itself as an institution

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:37.920
in the business of enchantment,

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.800
can make you forget the immense
and ever growing choke hold

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.750
over the entertainment industry.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.640
And it's obviously not just preaching

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:46.770
the gospel of Mickey for fun.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.247
As Giroux furthers,

00:16:48.247 --> 00:16:50.100
"That Disney has a political stake

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.290
in creating a particular moral order

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:53.880
favorable to its commercial interest

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.010
raises questions about what it teaches."

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:58.710
He argues that the lesson
plans at the school of Disney,

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:02.040
ultimately "reinforce an
infantalized and privatized

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.510
notion of citizenship."

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:06.750
Disney probably isn't consciously
trying to mimic religion,

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.850
but its approach to converting acolytes

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.710
can border on indistinguishable.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.640
Let us repeat.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:15.120
Disney is not trying to be a religion,

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:18.540
but it's tactics and the
reception it receives from fans,

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.210
often takes on a spiritual tinge.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:22.830
Disney's interests are well served

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:24.150
when people buy its products,

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:25.710
but its interests are best served,

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.480
when a consumption driven population

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.520
is more concerned with
having fun in Disney world

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.010
than say, with the labor
rights of the workers

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.230
making the park happen in the first place.

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:36.060
Or the company's serial coverups

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.160
of sexual harassment and assault.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.360
In our cynical day and age,

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.760
we all pretty much know
that giant corporations

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:44.190
basically never become giant corporations

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:47.460
because they've done things
in kind and magnanimous ways,

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.410
no matter how cute their mascot is.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.030
And Disney is no different,

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:53.940
while it's been hosting
gay days since 1991

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.370
under the auspice of
celebrating the queer community.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:58.890
It was also just recently
busted for donating money to

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.140
politicians who oppose queer rights.

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:04.080
That includes Florida
Republican, Dennis Baxley,

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:06.840
a career long champion
of anti-gay legislation,

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:09.540
and sponsor of the controversial
"Don't say gay" bill,

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.650
which limit school teachers

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.380
from mentioning anything queer
related in the classroom.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.840
While claiming to be a
pride friendly company,

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:18.120
they've simultaneously
been funding politicians

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.610
who are actively harming
the queer community.

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:22.260
Now after public outcry,

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:24.780
Disney CEO Bob Chapek,
eventually spoke out

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:28.200
against the bill promising
to be a better ally

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:29.760
and announce that the company was pausing

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.410
political donations in Florida,

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:34.500
yet concurrently queer Pixar
workers published a statement

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.600
claiming that Disney higher ups insisted

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:40.140
they cut nearly every moment
of overtly gay affection

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.100
in their films,

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:44.730
suggesting the company's
allyship remains suspect.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.860
And this is hardly the first of Disney's

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.780
questionable political affiliations.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.070
They've also funded business groups

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.800
who actively fight climate
change legislation.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:55.590
And a recent report found that 69%

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:56.880
of their political donations

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:59.370
went to anti-abortion politicians.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:03.210
It's rainbow capitalism
at its most insidious.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:04.710
Or take the time in 2013

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:06.840
as Disney was developing the movie Coco,

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.067
when they tried to trademark the phrase

00:19:09.067 --> 00:19:10.680
"Dia de Los Muertos".

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:13.470
This is part of Disney's
gargantuan merchandising machine,

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:16.260
which dates back to 1937's Snow White.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:17.190
You heard that right.

00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:18.630
In the lead up to the release

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.450
of their groundbreaking
celebration of Mexican culture,

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.670
Disney tried to actively snatch the name

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:26.310
of a sacred tradition outta
the hands of the Mexican people

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.490
across multiple media platforms.

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:30.570
It's not good, team.

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:31.710
It's not good.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.600
What's more the values espoused

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:34.950
in Disney films over the years

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.230
can leave a foul taste in the mouth

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:38.880
of a more progressive culture.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.620
From blatant racism,

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:43.299
to tired tropes of princesses
being rescued by princes,

00:19:43.299 --> 00:19:45.270
Disney has long been a protector

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:47.520
of white heteronormative ideology,

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.740
with much of the fantasy
that makes it so appealing

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:52.230
coming from a longing for an imagined past

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:53.460
of greater simplicity.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:56.190
Despite Disney's attempts to
keep its nostalgia apolitical

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:58.830
there's nonetheless a
deeply political tinge

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.590
to its avocation of a better time.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:04.440
Especially when you remember
that in this romanticized past,

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:07.680
many minority groups experienced
profound discrimination.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:09.990
And while Disney is certainly
getting better about depicting

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:11.100
more diverse stories.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.750
It's hard to outrun its legacy,

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.610
especially when those foundational films

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:17.130
and park attractions remain so popular.

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:20.490
So it looks like Disney has
successfully used aspects

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.740
of religion to maintain
its cultural power.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.390
But that doesn't mean

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:26.970
that it's intentionally built a religion.

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.860
At the same time, it's the epitome

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:30.440
of a capitalist institution

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:31.980
and has always been most loyal

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.620
to the creed of maximizing profits.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.320
So what exactly does that make it?

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:39.420
That question, like the
historic relationship

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.602
between capitalism and
religion in America,

00:20:41.602 --> 00:20:43.950
is more complicated than you might think.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:46.770
Dating back to the 16th
century Christian missionaries

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:49.890
who accompanied gold hungry
explorers on their excursions

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.960
to the new world.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.420
Religious scholar, Robert
Lawrence Moore argues

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.240
that religion has evolved
alongside mass consumer culture

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:01.140
out of necessity, increasingly
commodifying along the way,

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:03.900
he writes that, "Religious
influences established themselves

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.430
in the forms of commercial culture

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:07.230
that emerged in the 19th century,

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:10.020
turning the United States
into a flowering Eden

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:12.450
of leisure industries by
the middle of the 20th."

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.760
Beginning with various sex, mass produced

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.620
and extensive religious reading materials,

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.750
religions expanded their wares

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.700
by entering radio and theater,

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.740
and eventually television
via televangelist

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:25.290
like Jim and Tammy Faye
Baker, Pat Robertson,

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:26.490
and Jimmy Swaggart.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:29.220
They expanded beyond halls
of worship into nonprofits,

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.490
athletic clubs, like the
YMCA, social halls, and so on.

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.640
He explains that, "By
degrees, religion itself

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:38.250
took on the shape of a
commodity as it looked for ways

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.160
to appeal to all consumers,
using the techniques

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.230
of advertising and publicity."

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:44.190
At the same time,

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.530
religious institutions
have been notably exempt

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.270
from some of the governmental regulations

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:50.010
and limitations of other markets.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:53.610
Moore notes, rightly
that flashing neon signs

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:55.740
promising "Jesus Saves"

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.950
would never get churches in
trouble for false advertising.

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:00.150
After World War II,

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.550
comodified religion poured
into American culture

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:04.350
at an unprecedented rate,

00:22:04.350 --> 00:22:06.270
and culture responded in like

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:08.760
with a proliferation of
Hollywood blockbusters

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.620
based on biblical stories.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:12.870
Around this time, America
saw the beginnings

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:15.270
of the megachurch, which
according to scholar,

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:17.970
Scott Thumma function like corporations,

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:20.370
with the pastor as the often handsome

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:22.830
and handsomely compensated CEO.

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:24.990
They brand themselves
like corporations too,

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.810
by offering disparate
attractive forms of fun,

00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:30.120
performing arts, recreation
activities, gyms,

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:31.410
even movie theaters.

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:33.238
And don't even get us started again

00:22:33.238 --> 00:22:36.360
on the enormous Christian music scene.

00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:38.010
And it wasn't just Christianity.

00:22:38.010 --> 00:22:40.590
From the sixties on,
hundreds of new age religions

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:42.930
flourished among free thinking boomers,

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:45.000
almost always with economic tie-ins

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.360
in the form of healing, spas,
crystals, and radio stations.

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:51.277
And this way as sociologists
Peter L. Berger has observed,

00:22:51.277 --> 00:22:54.030
"Religious institutions
become marketing agencies

00:22:54.030 --> 00:22:56.790
and the religious traditions
become consumer commodities.

00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:59.250
And the good deal of
religious activity comes to be

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:01.890
dominated by the logic
of market economies."

00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:04.260
In recent years, as Mazur and Koda note,

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:05.940
the line between religious activities

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:09.090
and commercial activities has
become increasingly blurry,

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:11.610
with unexpected crossovers
between the two realms

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.320
and everything from Christian MLMs

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.880
to Jewish dating sites.

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:17.670
Increasingly people like the
fourth best Hollywood Chris,

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:20.310
will identify not as
religious, but as spiritual,

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:22.170
a term that is inherently looser

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:24.570
and can be conducive to a
sort of grab bag approach

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:25.710
to spirituality.

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:27.570
Mazur and Koda concur.

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:28.537
Writing of Disney,

00:23:28.537 --> 00:23:31.380
"They have entered the market
at a time when many people

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:33.210
are not only searching for alternatives

00:23:33.210 --> 00:23:34.500
to traditional religion,

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:37.170
but are also flexible
with what they find."

00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:39.660
So maybe the answer
ultimately is that Disney

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:41.520
is fulfilling functions of religion,

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:44.010
such as religious institutions
fulfill functions,

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:45.390
like fun and entertainment

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:47.550
that are typically associated with Disney.

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:51.990
So Disney's not necessarily
becoming more like religion.

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:55.800
Religion might just be
becoming more like Disney.

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.600
And nowhere is this bizarre paradox,

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:59.310
more apparent than at
one of the countries,

00:23:59.310 --> 00:24:01.410
many Jesus themed parks.

00:24:01.410 --> 00:24:03.810
But then again, maybe
we shouldn't see this

00:24:03.810 --> 00:24:07.020
as strange at all because
capitalism as an economic theory,

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:10.230
has actually never been
totally free from religion.

00:24:10.230 --> 00:24:12.787
Philosopher at Walter
Benjamin, famously said that,

00:24:12.787 --> 00:24:15.120
"A religion may be
discerned in capitalism.

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:18.210
That is to say capitalism
serves essentially to allay

00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:21.739
the same anxieties,
torments, and disturbances

00:24:21.739 --> 00:24:24.990
to which the so-called
religions offered answers."

00:24:24.990 --> 00:24:27.690
Which basically means that capitalism

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:29.550
isn't just an economic system,

00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:32.970
but a set of beliefs that aims
to offer meaning and purpose

00:24:32.970 --> 00:24:33.840
to modern life.

00:24:33.840 --> 00:24:37.350
But rather than offering the
hope peace and justice often

00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:39.570
promised by religion,
according to Benjamin,

00:24:39.570 --> 00:24:42.240
capitalism, "is a religion which offers us

00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:45.300
not the reform of existence,
but its complete destruction.

00:24:45.300 --> 00:24:48.558
It is the expansion of despair
until despair becomes a

00:24:48.558 --> 00:24:52.110
religious state of the world
in the hope that this will lead

00:24:52.110 --> 00:24:53.280
to salvation."

00:24:53.280 --> 00:24:56.437
In this context, all kinds
of profit driven institutions

00:24:56.437 --> 00:24:58.830
could be seen as doing something similar,

00:24:58.830 --> 00:25:01.800
i.e. offering their own
solutions to problems

00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:04.230
previously thought to be
the realm of religion.

00:25:04.230 --> 00:25:06.840
Whether you're preserving
your Hello Kitty lunch box

00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:08.040
behind a wall of glass,

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:09.240
or worshiping at the altar

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:10.770
of your favorite CrossFit instructor,

00:25:10.770 --> 00:25:12.480
praying with your model hot pastor

00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:13.950
at an evangelical megachurch,

00:25:13.950 --> 00:25:16.710
or spending your whole paycheck
at Disney's Animal Kingdom,

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:19.200
which why, it's the
saddest place in the world

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:20.730
because it's like a zoo,

00:25:20.730 --> 00:25:23.190
but there's no way
they're taking care of it

00:25:23.190 --> 00:25:24.390
the same way you would take care of a zoo.

00:25:24.390 --> 00:25:25.590
It's really, it makes me feel bad.

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:27.930
Don't go to Animal Kingdom no matter what

00:25:27.930 --> 00:25:30.720
just about every major
institution you're engaging with

00:25:30.720 --> 00:25:32.400
is inevitably shining their lights

00:25:32.400 --> 00:25:34.650
towards the goodness of our one true God.

00:25:34.650 --> 00:25:35.640
Capital.

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:38.970
And as for Disney adults,
are they part of a religion?

00:25:38.970 --> 00:25:41.310
Nah, not by our estimations,

00:25:41.310 --> 00:25:44.580
but are they an excellent
example of the porousness between

00:25:44.580 --> 00:25:46.230
consumerism and spirituality

00:25:46.230 --> 00:25:48.600
that characterizes this moment in time?

00:25:48.600 --> 00:25:49.920
Almost certainly.

00:25:49.920 --> 00:25:52.260
But the good thing is, unless
you're the type of person

00:25:52.260 --> 00:25:54.390
who uses up all your yearly vacation days

00:25:54.390 --> 00:25:57.900
for trips to Anaheim and
Orlando, you are in the clear.

00:25:57.900 --> 00:26:00.210
I guess, unless you're
really into Star Wars.

00:26:00.210 --> 00:26:01.800
'Cause that's that's Disney now.

00:26:01.800 --> 00:26:04.830
Or if you've enjoyed
the 29 or so MCU movies

00:26:04.830 --> 00:26:06.630
and the growing number of MCU TV shows,

00:26:06.630 --> 00:26:09.810
